description.narrative:
At the annual Assembly of the Parties meeting in november 2024, the new multiannual IDLO strategic framework 2025 - 2028 was approved by member states, including Sweden. At the same time, the first management plan 2025-2026 was approved. The strategic framework includes the following;
Vision: A world in which every person lives in dignity and equality under the rule of law
Mission: Champion people centered justice and promote the rule of law to advance sustainable development and help build more peaceful, inclusive and resilient societies
Strategic goal: Rule of law accelerates progress towards peace and sustainable development.
As an overarching theory of change, 5 pathways of change (levers) using both a top-down and a bottom up approach are defined;
- Legal and policy reform in partner countries - Strengthening institutions - Digital solutions - Participatory governance - Legal empowerment (of people living in poverty or oppression)
Outcomes are foreseen in 6 areas;
- Access to justice is expanded with a focus on vulnerable groups - Public integrity and anti-corruption efforts are enhanced - Justice gap for women and children is reduced - Action on climate justice and environmental governance is accelerated - Enabling environments for inclusive economic growth are promoted
In addition, IDLO continues to advocate globally, regionally and nationally for the rule of law and SDG 16 and it will communicate the value of rule of law for sustainable development and peace drawing on its program results, research and advocacy.
The plan also includes goals for enabling factors;
- Mobilizing political and financial support - Organizational systems and capacities
